\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {C.1}{\ignorespaces Over-crediting bias $\Delta = \mathrm  {AUC}_{\text  {raw}} - \mathrm  {AUC}_{\text  {opp-adj}}$ over the volume-dispersion $\times $ base-rate grid (synthetic). The bias increases in $\mathrm  {CV}(T)$ and decreases in the adjudicated base rate, as Proposition~\ref {prop:inflation} predicts. The two real platforms are overlaid at their measured $(\mathrm  {CV}(T),\text  {base rate})$ coordinates: BEC ($\mathrm  {CV}=2.79$, base rate $3.9\%$) and the federal ComprasNet platform ($\mathrm  {CV}=3.79$, base rate $0.5\%$). Federal sits in a higher-$\Delta $ region---higher dispersion and a roughly seven-fold lower base rate both push toward more complete inflation. Synthetic simulation; only $\mathrm  {CV}(T)$ and the base rate are taken from data.}}{20}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
